From 6fdc031b82f8979a2782d83a8ddc931f1d882e80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:22:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Spike: one crown integral on the light field (with odelia
 0013)

ResourceSpline::crown_integral sums w_j phi(E(h s_j)) over a unit crown rule
with the canopy shape folded into the weights, and records one statement per
crown at an active scalar. It replaces the FF16 deep-crown rows, the FF16
average light and TF24 mean light, and deletes TF24's unused assimilation.
Under mean light the radiation-site floor no longer fires: the folded weights
sum to one, so a mean of floored points cannot fall below the floor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFsPxk1yy62LrcCbtZUVeB
